server/.venv/
server/**/__pycache__/**
Budgetoid/.idea/**
Budgetoid/Application/bin/
Budgetoid/Application/obj/
Budgetoid/Domain/bin/
Budgetoid/Domain/obj/
Budgetoid/Infrastructure/bin/
Budgetoid/Infrastructure/obj/
ClientApp/Elm/elm-stuff/
ClientApp/Elm/public/
BudgetoidApp/Application/obj/
BudgetoidApp/Application/bin/
BudgetoidApp/Application/obj/
BudgetoidApp/Domain/obj/
BudgetoidApp/Domain/bin/
BudgetoidApp/Infrastructure/obj/
BudgetoidApp/Infrastructure/bin/
BudgetoidApp/Domain/obj/
BudgetoidApp/Domain/bin/

BudgetoidApp/.idea/**
/ClientApp/angular-budgetoid/.angular
/ClientApp/angular-budgetoid/dist
/ClientApp/angular-budgetoid/node_modules
/ClientApp/angular-budgetoid/public/assets/app-config.local.json

# Root tooling
/node_modules/
/package-lock.json
.pithos.d/

# Azurite storage emulator data
__azurite_db_*.json
__blobstorage__/
__queuestorage__/

# IDE run configurations
.run/
# Leading **/ on purpose: a pattern with a slash in the middle is anchored to this
# file's directory, and tooling writes these next to whatever directory it was
# invoked from — a stray .claude/logs turns up under docs/ or any other subtree.
**/.claude/grimoire/sessions/
**/.claude/logs/

# azd-synthesized infra (generated from the Aspire AppHost, which is the source of
# truth). azd regenerates it at provision/deploy time; committing it would drift.
/infra/
/BudgetoidApp/AppHost/infra/

CLAUDE.local.md
# Same leading **/ as the two rules above, and for the same reason: subagents write
# their memory next to the directory they were working in, so it lands under
# BudgetoidApp/ or ClientApp/ rather than at the root. A root-anchored rule caught
# none of those, and they were committed by accident twice.
**/.claude/agent-memory/
/.claude/skills/grimoire.*
/.claude/agents/grimoire.*
/.claude/grimoire.json

# Backlog tooling — both skills drive the private budgetoid-specs repository and the
# personal GitHub Project, so they are useful only to an account that can reach those.
/.claude/skills/budgetoid.publish-backlog/
/.claude/skills/budgetoid.story-context/

# Pending hardening backlog — lives in the private budgetoid-specs repository,
# because a public list of unclosed weaknesses is a map.
TECH_DEBT.md

# Same rule, same reason: a working list of the places the schema is not yet covered
# is the same map under a different name.
/PLAN.md

# Specifications for capabilities that do not exist yet. docs/ documents only what is
# true today, and agreed-but-unbuilt design lives in the private budgetoid-specs
# repository until the day it ships.
/SRS-*.md
/SPEC-*.md
/USER-STORIES.md

# Personal tooling that drives this checkout rather than the product: the grimoire CLI
# and its manifest belong to whoever installed them, not to the repository.
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/.pithos
/.pi/
